't say the actors didn't enjoy  themselves olson isn't a fan of thrill  rides like roller coasters but she loves  a good flying stunt but all this hanging  about just looks super uncomfortable to  us  number five betany spent a lot of time  in the air fighting the guest appearance  he teased to the world he'd said he was  thrilled to be working with an actor  that he respected and that he was proud  of the hard work they'd done together  that actor was of course himself he  trolled the entire world but he still  did good work we won't discount it and  having an authentic fight with yourself  is hard just ask captain america  number six of course it takes a ton of  editing to put two betanise on the  screen at the same time but did you know  there was more cgi in one division than  in endgame given the show has eight hour  long episodes and end game is only three  hours perhaps that's reasonable but we  can cut that down to seven hours of cgi  because almost every effect used in the  first episode was done practically  number seven except for the choking  scene this was the first glimpse we had  into wandavision that not everything was  as it seems the scene was incredibly fun  for deborah joe rupp but also difficult  to do she kept asking wait what you want  me to do what no i don't get it wait  what it also broke out of the sitcom  style with the moment vision reaches  into the throat of mr heart and stops  him from choking they had a live  audience for this scene and one thing  you just can't do is break the fourth  wall because there's not a fourth wall  to break and yet for just a moment there  is when we get a glimpse of paul's face  number eight and the live audience was a  different experience for the cast it  feels very different you have to swing  for the fences as jess hall put it as if  things weren't complicated enough now  you're doing a 26 minute single take in  front of a live audience effectively  essentially filmed theater it was filmed  in front of a live audience which was  just bananas number nine while olson  wasn't going so far as to slip on banana  peels for the laugh she did manage to  take it too far once she turned a double  take into a triple take which is when  the director finally said that's it i've  had enough you've gone too far elizabeth  a triple take what a ridiculous concept  elizabeth was proud to have that moment  to have finally earned her that's too  much badge  number 10 and in the realm of things  being just too much kat dennings avoided  a close call when she'd spoken up about  just recovering from an injury to her  foot that left her in a boot uncertain  she could do a run across the field she  said here's the thing i'll do it i can't  guarantee my ankle will make it to  tomorrow so they brought in a stunt  person to do it for her  number 11. you know who didn't think  they'd ever be brought in again paul  bettany he went through a stressful  experience walking into the studio  thinking it was the end you know due to  his character being finished off in  endgame  only to find out about the new show  number 12. he wasn't the only one  feeling weird energy coming into the  show elizabeth was used to being able to  dissolve into an ensemble in the movies  to hear about wandavision she was  excited about the prospect of it but  intimidated to be taking up so much  screen time  number 13. no reason to fear when dick  van dyke is here he was brought in to  assist them through sitcom bootcamp  every decade of wandavision brought in  new challenges for the actors as quite  literally everything changed their  speech rhythm postures movement and  language all took a lot of work to  perfect for each era of tv olsen  clarified that it isn't specific to the  time it's specific to the sitcoms of the  time in the 70s there was a relaxation  of women and their behavior on tv which  changed everything for her character  number 14 except for that moment where  she had to go back in time as scarlet  witch when she first landed the job  olson was promised she would never need  to wear the original costume and that  promise was broken however given she  looked better than bethany there were no  complaints from her  number 15 it's not easy being betany he  had an incredibly long makeup process  which they managed to work down for the  tv show or they never would have gotten  anything accomplished 10 hours into  costume eight hours out not possible for  one division  number 16. another near impossibility  was crafting up witch runes trying to  get the look of the runes just right was  taxing on the artists because their  first attempt looked just too similar to  the wakandan alphabet and not witchy  enough  number 17. and what struggles might  catherine han have playing a witch the  shooting for agatha all along had to be  planned well in advance because it would  have been a nightmare to return to all  these locations for three second clips  so at the end of filming each decade  they would grab the shots they needed  number 18 jumping from decade to decade  may have been impressive but it wasn't  the most impressive thing betany and  olson's standout moments happened when  they were just together connecting and  sparkling the goodbye was a  heartbreaking scene and a tough one  emotionally so said director matt  shakman so they gave themselves a lot of  extra time to film it because it was  tricky to pull off  number 19 what was tricky for everyone  was coming up with the perfect words to  describe the importance of grief they  landed on what is grief if not love  persevering thanks to a final line tweak  from paul bettany the other struggle  with this scene was having vision come  off sympathetic and not preachy  number 20 it wasn't hard for paul to  sympathize with wanda's experience he  tragically lost his brother to a car  crash which helped him connect to the  show's message and bring a more  authentic understanding and performance  wandavision is worth a re-watch if  you're considering it now is a great  time with doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness in theaters did  wandavision bring out the nostalgia in  you what sitcoms were you watching on tv  that it reminded you of let us know in  the comments and thanks for hanging out  with us here at the things

